{#- The Texas pilot page moved to /partners/. GitHub Pages has no server
    redirects, so each old address is a real page (HTTP 200, which ad
    platforms need from a landing URL) that sends the visitor on and carries
    the query string (gclid, fbclid, utm_*) and #hash with it. Zoho's
    after-booking redirect still points at /TexasPartners/booked/ until it is
    changed in Zoho, so that one must keep working, including inside the
    calendar frame. Other spellings (/texaspartners/, /Partners/) are caught
    by 404.njk. Data: src/_data/legacyPartnerRedirects.json. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Moved to {{ r.to }}</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ r.to }}" />
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ r.to }}" />
  <script>location.replace('{{ r.to }}' + location.search + location.hash);</script>
</head>
<body><p>This page moved to <a href="{{ r.to }}">{{ site.url }}{{ r.to }}</a>.</p></body>
</html>
